000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. RPTDATE.
000300* A special register first named in the REPORT SECTION (SOURCE
000400* TALLY) is an ordinary item, not a record of file 0: it once
000500* turned the input file variable-length, and the records were
000600* read four bytes early (#34). Expected output recorded from IBM
000700* ANS COBOL on TK5.
000800 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
000900 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001000 FILE-CONTROL.
001100     SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE.
001200     SELECT PRINT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-PROUT.
001300 DATA DIVISION.
001400 FILE SECTION.
001500 FD  IN-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
001600 01  IN-REC.
001700     05  IN-NAME PIC X(10).
001800     05  FILLER  PIC X(70).
001900 FD  PRINT-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED REPORT IS DATE-RPT.
002000 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002100 01  EOF PIC X VALUE 'N'.
002200 REPORT SECTION.
002300 RD  DATE-RPT PAGE LIMIT IS 20 LINES HEADING 1 FIRST DETAIL 3.
002400 01  TYPE PH LINE 1.
002500     05  COLUMN 1  PIC X(6)  VALUE 'TALLY '.
002600     05  COLUMN 8  PIC 9(5)  SOURCE TALLY.
002700 01  DL TYPE DETAIL LINE PLUS 1.
002800     05  COLUMN 1  PIC X(10) SOURCE IN-NAME.
002900 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
003000     OPEN INPUT IN-FILE OUTPUT PRINT-FILE.
003100     INITIATE DATE-RPT.
003200     READ IN-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
003300     PERFORM SHOW UNTIL EOF = 'Y'.
003400     TERMINATE DATE-RPT.
003500     CLOSE IN-FILE PRINT-FILE.
003600     STOP RUN.
003700 SHOW.
003800     DISPLAY 'READ [' IN-NAME ']'.
003900     GENERATE DL.
004000     READ IN-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
